From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:05:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Split stdio MCP from the TCP bridge; forward sandbox in the
 CLI

Problem: the v1 port tied the whole MCP server, Tokio and the TCP bridge to
  one `mcp` feature and built AROS without it. On x86_64 ABIv11 only Tokio's
  `net` (mio, socket2) fails to compile; the runtime, timers, sync and stdio
  parts do not need it. The CLI also declared its automation dependency
  without default features and did not forward `sandbox`, so a default CLI
  build silently fell back to the unconfined plain std::fs roots (host
  tests show the fallback lets symlinks escape the granted root).
Rationale: `mcp` = rmcp + Tokio without networking (stdio server and the
  bridge protocol client); `bridge` = Tokio TCP transport; `sandbox` =
  cap-std. The bridge client takes an injected Connector so a target can
  supply its own transport; without one, a call fails before anything is
  sent and `mcp --bridge` is refused up front. Upstream defaults are kept
  (mcp + bridge + sandbox), so other platforms build as before. Bridge tests
  that need a TCP fake app are gated on `bridge`.
Scope: crates/automation, apps/photocraft-cli features and bridge transport.
Upstream-status: candidate (feature split and connector seam are generic).
Prerequisites: 0001.
Verification: host tests: automation default 58+ suites ok; mcp+sandbox
  without bridge ok; mcp alone fails exactly the two symlink-escape tests
  (the documented plain std::fs weakness); CLI default ok.
Removal: when Tokio networking works on AROS and upstream has the split.
